# A tester's crash on Aridia (0.1.17, Quest 3S): with Akimbo, the game made a hand item while the left hand led, and the
# decode of its model went into the buffer the right hand's item kept aside was drawn from; that item came back to the
# hand with another's model, and the next change of item (the right grip) read garbage for its animation. Here the
# Blaster is in the right hand and the Swingshot in the left (QUEST_SIM_GIVE=15,12,16 QUEST_SIM_HOLD=15
# QUEST_SIM_LEFT=12), and QUEST_TEST_LEAD_SWITCH=16 asks for the Pyrocitor on each lead's third tick. Expect no crash,
# "[vr-akimbo] the game changed the hand's slot while the left hand led: the lead ends", the Blaster back in the right
# hand and firing, and the grip's wrench and the trigger's gun after it. With OPENRAC_ITEMS_DEBUG=1 the port says
# which buffer each decode went into; with OPENRAC_ITEMS_NO_RESTORE=1 (the old way) the mod's guard empties a
# spoilt slot instead ("its model was decoded over by another").
